# Supabase backend (client). The anon key is meant to be public — Row Level
# Security in the database is what protects the data, not key secrecy. Set both
# in Vercel and redeploy. Until they're set, the app still boots and the swipe →
# archetype → share flow works; auth/matches/chat just won't function.
# See supabase/README.md for the one-time project setup + schema.sql.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# There is intentionally no VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here. Vite inlines VITE_*
# vars into the client bundle, so a paid LLM API key behind that prefix would
# ship to every visitor's browser and be fully extractable via devtools. Until
# recommendations are served through a backend proxy that holds the key
# server-side, src/lib/api.js's getRecommendations() always returns the
# curated fallback set. Do not add VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY back without also
# adding that proxy.

# Web Push VAPID public key (safe to expose client-side — VAPID public keys are
# meant to be public). Required for ProfileScreen's "Enable notifications" to
# actually subscribe to push (src/lib/push.js). Generate a pair with
# `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`; the private half goes on the server only.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=

# ─── Server-side (NOT client env — do NOT VITE_-prefix these) ────────────────
# Set on the Vercel push function (api/notify.js). It reads a user's stored
# push_subscription with the service-role key, then sends a VAPID-signed push.
# These never reach the browser bundle. See supabase/README.md + api/notify.js.
#   SUPABASE_URL              = https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY = <service-role key — SECRET>
#   VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY          = <must be the SAME public key as VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY>
#   VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY         = <private half of the pair — SECRET>
#   VAPID_SUBJECT             = mailto:you@yourdomain.com
